# MTT Preprojection Repair Calculus

This repository is an isolated research laboratory for testing whether the
current Modal Triplet Theory (MTT) program can be simplified upstream of its
q79, Standard Model, quantum-mechanical, and gravitational realizations.

It does not modify MTT authority. It asks whether several difficult downstream
contracts are shadows of a smaller preprojection object.

## Research question

Can one typed repair system generate the accepted MTT structures through
certified projections?

```text
stratified admissible configuration object
  + internal curved superconnection family
  + scalar closure cost and outer Witten complex
  + central differential line
  + cyclic and configuration-space pairings
  + restricted symmetry/descent groupoid
                       |
                       v
       Hessians, kernels, fixed points, graphs,
       spinors, finite carriers, records and q79 shadows
```

## Non-interference rule

The q79 workers remain authoritative for q79 calculations. This repository may
read their promoted results but must not edit their repositories, consume their
work-in-progress packets as authority, or promote an MTT claim without the
bridge gates in [docs/PROMOTION_PROTOCOL.md](docs/PROMOTION_PROTOCOL.md).

## Initial workstreams

1. Test whether physical states may be stable nonzero-defect critical points.
2. Test whether squaring the first-order closure charge erases phase data.
3. Test whether Circle-Lens-Nil, qutrit Weyl data, the quarter-turn action, and
   the 27-state carrier share one central-extension representation.
4. Define a branch-independent category of admissibility germs.
5. Treat q79 as a candidate realization and construct a typed bridge only after
   the branch-independent object is stable.

The current leading synthesis is documented in
[docs/CANDIDATE_COMPARISON.md](docs/CANDIDATE_COMPARISON.md). It distinguishes
established mathematical ingredients from the still-open MTT same-source and
physical-selection theorem.

The first exact local same-source contraction is `H4-T1`, documented in
[theorems/PREPROJECTION_RESTRICTED_NESTED_REPAIR_TRANSFER_THEOREM_v1.md](theorems/PREPROJECTION_RESTRICTED_NESTED_REPAIR_TRANSFER_THEOREM_v1.md).
Its
[H4-T2 companion](theorems/PREPROJECTION_NONCENTRAL_CURVED_TRANSFER_AND_TERMINATION_THEOREM_v1.md)
gives an exactly terminating noncentral curved transfer.
The
[H4-T3 companion](theorems/PREPROJECTION_POSITIVE_NONCENTRAL_NESTED_TRANSFER_THEOREM_v1.md)
combines positive noncentral curvature with the same nested strict shadows.
The
[H4-T4 theorem](theorems/PREPROJECTION_STRICT_UNITAL_CURVATURE_AS_COEFFICIENT_THEOREM_v1.md)
completes its finite curved `A_infinity` extension without an infinite
curvature-insertion series.
The
[H4-T5 theorem](theorems/PREPROJECTION_TWISTED_MORITA_OVERLAP_DESCENT_AND_RANK102_COMPILER_THEOREM_v1.md)
globalizes that package through projective qutrit overlaps in twisted-Morita
form and composes it structurally with the typed q79 rank-102 Cech compiler.
The
[H4-T6 theorem](theorems/PREPROJECTION_Q79_HIRSCH_EXTENSION_TRANSFER_AND_INTERACTION_LOCATION_THEOREM_v1.md)
constructs the selected q79 rational topology factor itself. Its exact cyclic
contraction is strict, locating higher interactions in the twisted
coefficient/repair sector rather than in bare Fu-Yau circle topology.
The
[H4-T7 theorem](theorems/PREPROJECTION_BHT_TRANSPORTED_METRIC_AND_POLAR_OBSTRUCTION_THEOREM_v1.md)
proves the quantified non-isometric bridge: any bounded chain/product
transform has an exact transported metric, while physical mismatch is measured
by explicit chain commutators and polar product defects.
The
[H4-T8 theorem](theorems/PREPROJECTION_REPAIR_JET_TO_PERTURBATIVE_GRAPH_FUNCTOR_THEOREM_v1.md)
derives the Hessian, every repair-action vertex, reduced Euclidean propagator,
functional calculus and finite Wick graph weights from one residual-and-metric
jet, rather than accepting independent vertex tensors.
Its promotion requirements are frozen in
[docs/RESTRICTED_NESTED_REPAIR_MORPHISM_CONTRACT.md](docs/RESTRICTED_NESTED_REPAIR_MORPHISM_CONTRACT.md).

